etails_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "706023237bb74691", "kind": "experiment", "role": "Gm1", "tree_id": "e1:Gm1", "mission_id": "706023237bb74691", "facts": {"commit": "3d310fb015d0c7874f57c7cd5ad419760abc07d5", "base_commit": "9ad4e02526e0ed561c71716d317061ed4a0b2a02", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": ["164618338efd47c5", "806fdef9ee5b4dc6"], "source_count": 2, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.054594573403199634, "score": 0.8949092984982591}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "La combinaison conserve le parcours x contigu et les bases de lignes de T2, tout en distribuant les lignes (z,y) entre une équipe OpenMP persistante comme dans T1. Elle pourrait permettre le SIMD intra-ligne et le parallélisme inter-lignes sans recréer l’équipe à chaque pas; la barrière implicite de chaque boucle de travail préserve les dépendances entre les six pas. Les moyennes fournies pour T2 (0,0813 s) et T1 (0,2416 s) ne donnent pas de ventilation par budget de cœurs et ne prouvent pas que leurs gains s’additionnent; cette combinaison doit être mesurée aux budgets comparables d’un et quatre cœurs.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Conserver les bases de lignes z/y et les accès relatifs aux pointeurs de ligne de T2, avec une directive OpenMP SIMD sur x lorsque _OPENMP indique OpenMP 4.0 ou ultérieur; garder un chemin générique sinon.","Remplacer la boucle temporelle sérielle par une équipe OpenMP unique sur toute la durée des six pas et un partage statique collapse(2) des lignes z/y, en gardant x contigu.","Conserver la barrière implicite après chaque boucle de travail et l’alternance des deux tampons; dimensionner l’équipe avec le paramètre threads et ne pas imbriquer de région parallèle."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "f7e171e736ed48bd", "kind": "experiment", "role": "Gm2", "tree_id": "e1:Gm2", "mission_id": "f7e171e736ed48bd", "facts": {"commit": "c2a806307aa717cf98496391b06d499f3b085f9d", "base_commit": "c4a3af2c3be23347a691030547e4dec81defc32f", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": ["d96afbb4e38d4370", "e2e68740f1064099"], "source_count": 2, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.055090059187835744, "score": 0.8940565695389907}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Les bases de ligne et les pointeurs restrict de d96 peuvent faciliter l’auto-vectorisation des boucles x, tandis qu’une équipe OpenMP persistante évite de recréer le parallélisme à chaque pas. Les barrières entre pas restent nécessaires. Les mesures d’ensemble fournies sont de 0,080 s pour d96 et 0,220 s pour T1; elles ne démontrent ni l’addition des gains ni les résultats à un et quatre cœurs, que cette combinaison doit donc mesurer séparément.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Conserver les bases de ligne et les pointeurs restrict conditionnels de d96 dans le noyau, sans directive SIMD ni hypothèse d’alignement.","Ajouter une équipe OpenMP persistante et répartir les tranches z en plages contiguës déterministes selon la taille réelle de l’équipe, en conservant ces plages entre les pas.","Sélectionner les buffers selon la parité et synchroniser entre les pas dépendants; préserver les initialisations complètes, les bornes, la récurrence et les cas sans tranches intérieures."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "e2e68740f1064099", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T1", "tree_id": "e1:T1", "mission_id": "e2e68740f1064099", "facts": {"commit": "b3244455b50c8433e37a2aa46e40b9151738c400", "base_commit": "47e69a2108b11b6944d058afe08fffba262a9e2b", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.21989174622339427, "score": 0.6788948675804369}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "The three prior OpenMP candidates are all valid and have similar aggregate means (0.2379–0.2416 s), but the supplied observations do not establish a clear per-thread comparison. This candidate tests persistent ownership of contiguous z-slabs across six steps, with five explicit dependency barriers and no per-step worksharing dispatch. Stable slab ownership may reduce scheduling overhead or improve locality; coarse slabs may limit utilization at small sizes. Controller measurements at one and four threads, including initialization, are needed before drawing a performance conclusion.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Replace the serial timestep sweep with one OpenMP team whose requested size is capped by the positive threads budget and the number of interior z-slices.","Partition interior z-slices into deterministic contiguous per-thread ranges, keeping each thread on its slab for all six steps while traversing contiguous x positions.","Select input/output buffers by timestep parity and place an explicit barrier between dependent timesteps; rely on the parallel-region completion for the final step.","Preserve full initialization of both output buffers, the original stencil arithmetic, update bounds, and unchanged boundary behavior."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "469de416c9dc42cf", "kind": "experiment", "role": "T2", "tree_id": "e1:T2", "mission_id": "469de416c9dc42cf", "facts": {"commit": "e5b1e1b46558a71440ff75e0a75ef21d1ab4f638", "base_commit": "47e69a2108b11b6944d058afe08fffba262a9e2b", "parent_id": null, "source_ids": [], "source_count": 0, "source_change": {"available": true, "kind": "nonconfiguration_files_changed", "changed_file_count": 1, "configuration_file_count": 0, "semantic_novelty": "not_established_by_file_hashes", "identical_input_ids": [], "identical_input_count": 0}}, "measured_outcome": {"status": "valid", "correct": true, "mean_seconds": 0.08409908599967206, "score": 0.8468151879247069}, "diagnostic": "", "model_interpretation": {"claim": "Earlier reported means for row-base variants are close: 0.079497 s with explicit SIMD and 0.080044 s without it. This candidate hoists row bases and enables `omp simd` only when `_OPENMP` indicates OpenMP 4.0 or later, but adds no restrict/no-alias promise. It tests whether the SIMD hint and regular row accesses suffice without that extra promise. The ordinary loop remains for unsupported configurations and arbitrary widths; no alignment or ISA is assumed. No gain is presumed.", "transformations": "{"files":["src/candidate.cpp"],"retained":["Hoisted the center, neighboring-row, velocity, and destination bases outside the contiguous-x loop.","Added `omp simd` only under an OpenMP 4.0-or-newer compile-time guard; no explicit alignment or vector width is assumed, and the ordinary loop retains generic tail behavior.","Preserved the stencil recurrence, summation order, full initialization, boundaries, and timestep buffer alternation."]}", "applicability": "", "next_experiment": "", "evidence_ids": []}, "source_available": true, "details_are_bounded": true}, {"id": "656a1525dd